From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:49:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(documents): enforce tenant isolation on file bytes and
 bulk ZIP

Found by the disaster-recovery drill's tenant-isolation checks (and shown to
be PRE-EXISTING, not caused by restore: the document's tenantId was intact
in both the backup and the recovered database).

GET /documents/:id/file and POST /documents/bulk-download relied on
scope().tenantWhere(), which is `{}` in the default (legacy, non-pilot)
Prisma mode. Any authenticated user with documents:read could therefore
stream another tenant's attachment by id, and the bulk ZIP included other
tenants' files. The metadata endpoint (findOne) already gated on the owning
entity's tenant; the byte paths now use the same rule via a shared
isSameTenantAsCaller() helper (SUPER bypass unchanged; foreign ids answer
404 / are dropped from the ZIP before any storage read).

Drill: cross-tenant file access is now asserted on the source before the
backup and on the recovered application (single file + bulk ZIP); the
verify phase always runs schema parity and fails on any check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WtPBCrb8yTQgD6roYqdmPp
